  "correction_rules": [
    "Adjust forecasts downward when sentiment history shows negative bias (e.g., -0.25 or 0.00 in recent days) and true prices have been trending lower.",
    "Reduce forecast overshoots following sharp price spikes by applying a 10-15% dampening factor to the immediate next period’s forecast.",
    "When sentiment history includes a recent positive sentiment (e.g., 0.50), increase forecast sensitivity to recent price momentum, but cap upward adjustments at +5% to avoid overcorrection.",
    "Apply mean reversion correction: if forecast deviates >10% from 30-day moving average of true prices, adjust toward the average with a decay factor of 0.8 per period.",
    "For horizon >15 days, reduce forecast volatility by smoothing with a 5-day exponential moving average (EMA) of true prices, especially if sentiment is neutral or negative."
  ]
}
